(ned RACK CAL -- locate ONE fork: plunge over the taper, 4-side centre,)
(re-centre, verify deeper, retract. #1 = fork number for storage + prints)
(Globals in: _rc_cx _rc_cy predicted centre, _rc_safe / _rc_pfind / _rc_p60)
(work-Z levels, _rc_reach, feeds. Out: _rc_cx _rc_cy = FOUND centre, and)
(_rc_pfind reset to this tool top - 10 for the NEXT fork)
o<rc_locate> sub
  #<i> = #1

  G90
  G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
  G1 X[#<_rc_cx>] Y[#<_rc_cy>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]

  (Descend to the FIND level as a PROBE - early contact means off-centre.)
  (FIND HIGH, NOT DEEP - operator 2026-08-16: "its actually)
  (counterproductive to probe for the center so far down. the best place to)
  (probe is actually far up, so -20 from the parked position the first time,)
  (and therefacter, 10mm below the top of the previous tool". _rc_pfind)
  (carries that level: parked - 20 for the first fork, and each fork resets)
  (it to its own measured top - 10 for the one after it.)
  G38.3 Z[#<_rc_pfind>] F[#<_rc_fck>]
  o10 if [#5070 EQ 1]
    G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
    (abort, RACK CAL: contact while descending to the find level at fork #<i> - centre prediction is off, re-eyeball and restart from this fork)
  o10 endif

  (FIND, VERIFY, AND ON CONTACT FIND AGAIN LOWER - operator 2026-08-16:)
  (if during the dive it detects contact, go back up in Z until contact is)
  (lost and redo the zero finding at that level. The old code aborted here)
  (instead, which threw away a fork that was only slightly off-centre.)
  (WHY IT CONVERGES: the bore-to-taper clearance shrinks with depth, so a)
  (find done deeper is a tighter measurement than the one above it. Each)
  (pass centres at the deepest level that is still free, then tries the)
  (full depth again from that better centre.)
  #<tries> = 0
  #<fit>   = 0
  #<rise>  = 10.0
  #<clr>   = 1.0
  o40 while [[#<fit> EQ 0] AND [#<tries> LT 4]]
    (FAST PROBE SCALES WITH DEPTH - operator 2026-08-16: "as you go down)
    (low, the fast probe needs to be slowed down because it pushes the taper)
    (too much" ... "just make fast probe proportional to depth a linear)
    (combiantion between fast and slow probe speeds". Full #3004 at the top)
    (find level, falling linearly to #3005 at the deep verify level. Both)
    (ends are the operator's own numbers; nothing is invented between them.)
    (Recomputed INSIDE the loop, so a recovery re-find that happens lower)
    (down automatically probes slower than the first one did.)
    #<span> = [#<_rc_ptop> - #<_rc_p60>]
    o70 if [#<span> GT 0.001]
      #<frac> = [[#<_rc_ptop> - #<_z>] / #<span>]
    o70 else
      #<frac> = 0
    o70 endif
    o71 if [#<frac> LT 0]
      #<frac> = 0
    o71 endif
    o72 if [#<frac> GT 1]
      #<frac> = 1
    o72 endif
    #<_rc_fpr> = [#<_rc_fpr0> - [#<frac> * [#<_rc_fpr0> - #<_rc_fla>]]]
    (PRINT, RACK CAL fork #<i>: finding at Z#<_z> with fast probe #<_rc_fpr>)

    (4-sided find AT THE CURRENT Z: X pair first, then Y pair from the)
    (corrected X, so the Y touches are taken on a centred axis)
    o<rc_touch> call [0] [1]
    #<xp> = #<_rc_val>
    o<rc_touch> call [0] [-1]
    #<xm> = #<_rc_val>
    #<_rc_cx> = [[#<xp> + #<xm>] / 2]
    G1 X[#<_rc_cx>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
    o<rc_touch> call [1] [1]
    #<yp> = #<_rc_val>
    o<rc_touch> call [1] [-1]
    #<ym> = #<_rc_val>
    #<_rc_cy> = [[#<yp> + #<ym>] / 2]
    G1 X[#<_rc_cx>] Y[#<_rc_cy>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]

    (verify: the deep level must fit with NO touch)
    G38.3 Z[#<_rc_p60>] F[#<_rc_fck>]
    o30 if [#5070 EQ 0]
      #<fit> = 1
    o30 else
      (contact. Back UP until the probe opens - G38.5 stops on loss of)
      (contact - then a little more, and find again at THAT level.)
      #<ztouch> = #5063
      G91
      G38.5 Z[#<rise>] F[#<_rc_fla>]
      o60 if [#5070 EQ 0]
        G90
        G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
        (abort, RACK CAL: fork #<i> stayed in contact through a #<rise> mm retract - the spindle is jammed on the taper, not merely off-centre)
      o60 endif
      G1 Z[#<clr>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
      G90
      #<tries> = [#<tries> + 1]
      (PRINT, RACK CAL fork #<i>: fit touched at Z#<ztouch> - backed clear, re-centring at this level, try #<tries> of 4)
    o30 endif
  o40 endwhile

  o50 if [#<fit> EQ 0]
    G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]
    (abort, RACK CAL: fork #<i> still touching after 4 re-centres - centre not trusted, nothing stored for it)
  o50 endif
  (straight back to safety - no stop at 45 on the way out)
  G1 Z[#<_rc_safe>] F[#<_rc_ftr>]

  (Z: shoulder touch at THIS fork - every fork gets its own XYZ, no)
  (interpolation, no hardcoded end forks - operator 2026-08-04)
  o<rc_ztouch> call

  (THE NEXT FORK FINDS 10 MM BELOW THIS TOOL TOP. _rc_ztop is this fork's)
  (measured top in work coords, so the next fork starts from a level that)
  (was MEASURED rather than assumed.)
  #<_rc_pfind> = [#<_rc_ztop> - 10.0]

  (store MACHINE coords, all three together with the flag LAST: a fork is)
  (complete only if X Y AND Z landed)
  #<offx> = [#<_abs_x> - #<_x>]
  #<offy> = [#<_abs_y> - #<_y>]
  #<offz> = [#<_abs_z> - #<_z>]
  #[4100 + [#<i> * 4]]     = [#<_rc_cx> + #<offx>]
  #[4100 + [#<i> * 4] + 1] = [#<_rc_cy> + #<offy>]
  #[4100 + [#<i> * 4] + 2] = [#<_rc_ztop> + #<offz>]
  #[4100 + [#<i> * 4] + 3] = 1
  (PRINT, RACK CAL fork #<i>: X#<_rc_cx> Y#<_rc_cy> Ztop#<_rc_ztop> work - stored machine)
o<rc_locate> endsub
M2
